iOS Safari silently fails to trigger downloads when using `URL.createObjectURL()` due to security restrictions. Blob URLs work on other platforms but not iOS.

## Changes

**Added platform-aware download helper** (`Main.jsx:28-94`)
- `isIOS()`: Detects iOS devices via user agent + MacIntel touch detection for iPad Pro
- `blobToDataURL()`: FileReader-based Blob→Data URL conversion
- `triggerDownload()`: Routes to Data URL (iOS) or Blob URL (others)

**Updated download paths**
- `doGifExport()`: GIF downloads
- `doStaticExport()`: PNG downloads (regular + stickers)  
- `handleShare()`: Share fallback downloads

## Implementation

```javascript
async function triggerDownload(blob, filename) {
  const isiOS = isIOS();

  if (isiOS) {
    // iOS Safari: Use Data URL approach
    const dataUrl = await blobToDataURL(blob);
    const link = document.createElement("a");
    link.href = dataUrl;
    link.download = filename;
    // ... trigger download
  } else {
    // Other browsers: Use Blob URL with cleanup
    const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    // ... trigger download + revoke
  }
}
```

Non-iOS platforms preserve existing Blob URL behavior for performance. iOS gets Data URLs which work reliably on Safari.

